<title>SRI LANKA: Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</title>
<headline>Sri Lanka T-bill yields rise at weekly auction.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yields of three, six and 12-month Sri Lankan treasury bills rose at Wednesday's auction with six and twelve-month maturities being oversubscribed, the Central Bank said.</p>
<p>		  Bids received   Bids accepted   Avg yield</p>
<p>    3 months     3,504	     2,857	  17.85 (17.64)</p>
<p>    6 months	 220		 145	  17.85 (17.57)</p>
<p>    12 months    3,343	     2,330	  17.91 (17.73)</p>
<p>The Central Bank said it purchased treasury bills totalling 432 million rupees.</p>
<p>NOTE - Bids in millions of rupees, yields in percent (previous week's yields in brackets). --Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
